Lab 7: Manage Access to Private Automation Hub
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Create and configure user groups for different organizational roles in Private Automation Hub
Assign appropriate permissions to each user group based on role requirements
Implement proper access control mechanisms for automation content
Monitor user activities and audit access logs for security compliance
Understand best practices for managing user permissions in enterprise automation environments
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Linux command line operations
Familiarity with Ansible concepts and terminology
Knowledge of user and group management in Linux systems
Understanding of role-based access control (RBAC) principles
Basic knowledge of web-based administration interfaces
