Subtask 3.2: Enable Audit Logging
Access the system via SSH using the credentials provided in your lab environment.

Configure audit logging for the Private Automation Hub:

# Edit the galaxy configuration file
sudo vi /etc/pulp/settings.py

# Add or modify the following logging configuration
LOGGING = {
    'version': 1,
    'disable_existing_loggers': False,
    'formatters': {
        'verbose': {
            'format': '{levelname} {asctime} {module} {process:d} {thread:d} {message}',
            'style': '{',
        },
    },
    'handlers': {
        'audit_file': {
            'level': 'INFO',
            'class': 'logging.FileHandler',
            'filename': '/var/log/galaxy/audit.log',
            'formatter': 'verbose',
        },
    },
    'loggers': {
        'galaxy.audit': {
            'handlers': ['audit_file'],
            'level': 'INFO',
            'propagate': False,
        },
    },
}

# Enable audit logging
AUDIT_LOGGING_ENABLED = True
Create the log directory and set proper permissions:
sudo mkdir -p /var/log/galaxy
sudo chown pulp:pulp /var/log/galaxy
sudo chmod 755 /var/log/galaxy
Restart the galaxy services:
